/-!
# Packed annihilator and augmented inverse candidates

The first 109 annihilator rows, followed by coordinate rows 0 and 2,
form an invertible matrix. The coefficient vector selects the annihilator
polynomial. Its identification with that polynomial is a separate certificate.

Candidate generation and source attribution: `Kernel/source/GenerateKernel.py`
and `Kernel/source/README.md`. Every numerical assertion is checked in Lean.
-/

namespace Lyons.SimplicityCertificate.LocalCommutant.Kernel

open Atlas111WordCertificate

